# VolleySim determinism

`VolleySim` must be a pure function `(state, inputs) -> state`. godot-rollback-netcode replays it.

## Must

- Keep ALL match state in `sim.s` (ints/floats/bools/arrays/dicts only)
- Use only `+ - * /`, `sqrt`, `min/max/clamp/abs/sign`, `move_toward` on floats
- Derive FX/HUD from state (`*_serial`, `msg`, `phase`) in `MatchView`
- Add/adjust a test in `tests/cases/` for every rule change; run `godot --headless --path . --script res://tests/run_all.gd`

## Never

- `randf`/`randi`, `Time.*`, `OS.*`, node access, signals, tweens/timers, engine physics inside the sim
- `sin/cos/pow/log` or other libm calls (can differ per CPU)
- Fire FX or emit signals from inside `step()`
- Change sim constants/ordering without telling online players to update (peers must run the same build)
